meta {
  name: Unlinked Counts
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/clients/unlinked/counts
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

script:post-response {
  // The three totals, so the list requests below can assert they agree.
  // Runtime-only vars (never persisted to disk).
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    const body = res.getBody();
    bru.setVar("unlinkedPolicyCount", body.policies);
    bru.setVar("unlinkedContactCount", body.contacts);
    bru.setVar("unlinkedHouseholdCount", body.households);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns exactly the three numbers the chips show", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(Object.keys(body).sort()).to.eql([
      "contacts",
      "households",
      "policies",
    ]);
    expect(body.policies).to.be.a("number");
    expect(body.contacts).to.be.a("number");
    expect(body.households).to.be.a("number");
  });

  test("counts are never negative", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    for (const key of ["policies", "contacts", "households"]) {
      expect(body[key]).to.be.at.least(0);
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /clients/unlinked/counts

  The three numbers behind the **Unlinked** tab's filter chips on the Clients
  page (PAC-91 §10).

  - **Module:** `clients`
  - **Permission:** `clients:read` — **not** the `clients:read` OR
    `crm_service:read` gate that `GET /households/:id` and `GET /policies/:id`
    carry. Those exist because one record renders inside a CRM ticket's drawer;
    this is a report about the state of the client book, and belongs to whoever
    works that book. A CSR holding only `crm_service:read` gets **403**.
  - **Data scope:** `own` collapses to **branch**, exactly as `GET /households`
    does — client records are shared and carry no per-user owner.

  ## Response
  ```json
  { "policies": 135, "contacts": 280, "households": 59 }
  ```

  Each number is the `total` of the matching `GET /clients/unlinked?kind=…`
  page, computed from the same filter, so a chip can never disagree with the
  list behind it.

  ## Why a separate endpoint rather than `?kind=summary`
  The page shows all three counts whichever list is open, so they are a
  different question with a different cache lifetime — and a paginated envelope
  with no `items` would have made every field of the response shape optional for
  the three real kinds.

  ## What each number means
  | Field | Predicate |
  |---|---|
  | `policies` | `policies` with no `householdId` |
  | `contacts` | `contacts` with no **current** row in `householdMembers` (`endedAt: null`) |
  | `households` | `households` with no `primaryContactId` |

  All three exclude `isTestRecord` rows — the agency's Sample/Test records were
  flagged in PAC-91 Phase 1 and must never be presented as work.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | `clients` disabled for the agency, or the caller lacks `clients:read` |
}
